<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of United Mountaineers of the North Caucasus and Dagestan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Union of the United Mountaineers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of United Mountaineers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a> was a political organisation founded at a congress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a> in May 1917, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a>. It brought together representatives of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechens">Chechens</a>, Ingush, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetians">Ossetians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabardians">Kabardians</a>, Dagestanis and other mountain peoples to seek self-government. Its central committee became the government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</a> proclaimed in 1918.</p></div>
